28/2022 through 06/30/2022, HCPCS code J3590 should be used to report Faricimab-svoa (Vabysmo™) for Part A services. Effective for dates of service 1/28/2022 through 09/30/2022, HCPCS code J…","2":"Intravitreal injection code","3":"Via SUSVIMO drug implant only"},"covered":{"1":"Ranibizumab and biosimilars ranibizumab-nuna and ranibizumab-eqrn HCPCS Codes Q5124, Q5128, Q5155, J0177, J2778, Q5168 should be reported with the ICD-10-CM codes in Group 1 below.","2":"HCPCS codes J0178 EYLEA® (aflibercept), Q5147 , Aflibercept, PAVBLU™ (aflibercept-ayyh), Q5150 AHZANTIVE®(aflibercept-mrbb), Q5153 OPUVIZ™aflibercept-yszy, Q5170 Eydenzelt® (aflibercept-boav) should be reported with the ICD-10-CM codes- Group 2 below. HCPCS code Q5149 -ENZEEVU™(aflibercept-abzv) is only indicated for the treatment of patients with Neovascular (Wet) Age-Related Macular Degeneration (AMD)*. Only the ICD-10-CM codes with an asterisk reflect the indication. HCPCS code Q5155 -YESAFILI™(aflibercept-jbvf) is indicated for the treatment of patients with Macular Edema following Retinal Vein Occlusion, Diabetic Macular Edema and Diabetic Retinopathy","3":"HCPCS code J0179 Brolucizumab-dbll and Q5149 -ENZEEVU™(aflibercept-abzv) should be reported with the ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes- Group 3 below.","4":"HCPCS code J2777 -Faricimab-svoa (Vabysmo™) and J0177 - EYLEA®HD (aflibercept), should be reported with the ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes below-Group 4.","5":"HCPCS code J0177 Aflibercept HD should be reported with the ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes- Group 5 below.","6":"HCPCS code J2779 SUSVIMO should be reported with the ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes-Group 6 below."},"noncovered":{}}}]